    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="0630" n="486" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg486"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Kreutzin, Mathias/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-17T15:00:00+08:00">November 17, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 17—10:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>67. My 65 [<hi rendition="#italic">66</hi>], November 15, 1 p.m.<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d481-f1"/> Ransom has been reduced to $6,000 Mexican, $60 to be paid
                    immediately for subsistence for Father Kreutzin. Sixty dollars sent by
                    messenger. Three hundred soldiers were sent from Tayeh to Tawangtien, but on
                    arrival there found town deserted and Father Kreutzin removed elsewhere.
                    Catholic Fathers here feel confident he will be released in a few days. Letter
                    received by them yesterday from bandit chief states Father Kreutzin well and
                    that he will be delivered over unharmed on payment of reduced ransom. A Father
                    from Wuchang has gone to Tayeh authorized to pay a maximum of $1,500 not as
                    ransom but expense money to effect release. I am pressing Chinese authorities
                    daily on case and they are lending cooperation. Legation informed.<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d481-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d481-f1" n="14" xml:id="d481-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d481-f2" n="15" xml:id="d481-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 72, November 30, the Consul General at Hankow reported to the
                    Department that “Mission authorities state bandits have agreed to release Father
                    Kreutzin for $3,000. Money will be sent by messenger from Tayeh at once”
                    (393.1111 Kreutzin, Mathias/37). The release and safe arrival at Tayeh of Father
                    Kreutzin was reported in telegram No. 73, December 2 (393.1111 Kreutzin,
                    Mathias/38).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
